 items; Ashok Shah and Shalin Shah are Directors on its board.\n- **Gujarat Natural Resources Limited** Engaged in oil & gas exploration; Ashok Shah is Director and Shalin Shah is Managing Director on its board.\n- **Lesha Ventures Private Limited** Engaged in non-specialized retail trade in stores; Ashok Shah is Director on its board.","src":"annual_report","as_of":"2018-01-31"},"end_markets":{"title":"End Markets (RHP)","body":"- Infrastructure and construction\n- Real estate\n- Tier-2 and tier-3 cities","src":"annual_report","as_of":"2018-01-31"},"demand_drivers":{"title":"Mdna (RHP)","body":"- Demand for TMT bars is driven by infrastructure, construction, and real estate projects, supported by government initiatives like 'Make in India', increased infrastructure spending, and urbanization.\n- Rising awareness around high-strength, earthquake-resistant TMT bars in residential and commercial construction is boosting market potential.\n- Shift towards organized supply chains and increased demand from tier-2 and tier-3 cities is opening new avenues for growth.\n- Price volatility in raw materials and finished steel products, driven by global market dynamics, can impact margins and planning.\n- Intense competition from unorganized local players and fluctuating seasonal construction demand pose risks to the outlook.\n- Outlook is positive, driven by sustained demand for TMT bars in infrastructure and real estate, supported by the manufacturing subsidiary and market expansion plans; diversification into chemical trading and potential strategic collaborations are expected to further enhance growth prospects.","src":"annual_report","as_of":"2018-01-31"},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- Volatility in raw material costs and finished steel product prices, influenced by global market dynamics and geopolitical factors, can affect both procurement and sales margins.\n- Changes in taxation, import/export policies and environmental regulations affecting the steel sector 